{"id":"92f7818d1e7f469c","group":"58","path":"58/batch19/58-df-torus.md","title":"Torus","display":"df-torus — Torus","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-torus","aliases":["58-df-torus","Torus"],"display":"df-torus — Torus","depends_on":["[[58-df-sphere]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-torus"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-torus</span><span>Torus</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-torus — Torus"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"ed44d43cf74ca35e\" href=\"?note=ed44d43cf74ca35e\" title=\"58-df-sphere\">58-df-sphere</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Explicit relation signatures used below: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Torus}_S\\subseteq V^{2}\">\\(\\mathrm{Torus}_S\\subseteq V^{2}\\)</span>.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n\\in\\omega\">\\(n\\in\\omega\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T\\in V\">\\(T\\in V\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"S^1\">\\(S^1\\)</span> is the unit circle supplied by <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"ed44d43cf74ca35e\" href=\"?note=ed44d43cf74ca35e\" title=\"58-df-sphere\">58-df-sphere</a></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Torus}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Torus}_S\\)</span> (torus predicate defined here)</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}torus}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{Torus}_S(T,n)\\leftrightarrow n\\in\\omega\\land T=(S^1)^n\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}torus}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{Torus}_S(T,n)\\leftrightarrow n\\in\\omega\\land T=(S^1)^n\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}torus\\text{-}notation}\\vdash\n\\mathbb T^n\\coloneqq(S^1)^n\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}torus\\text{-}notation}\\vdash\n\\mathbb T^n\\coloneqq(S^1)^n\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The identification <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb T^n\\cong\\mathbb R^n/\\mathbb Z^n\">\\(\\mathbb T^n\\cong\\mathbb R^n/\\mathbb Z^n\\)</span>, compactness, connectedness, the abelian group structure, and the homology and fundamental-group computations are downstream theorems.</li>\n<li>Character group: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\widehat{\\mathbb{T}^n} \\cong \\mathbb{Z}^n\">\\(\\widehat{\\mathbb{T}^n} \\cong \\mathbb{Z}^n\\)</span> (integer-valued characters)</li>\n<li>Fourier analysis: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L^2(\\mathbb{T}^n) = \\bigoplus_{k \\in \\mathbb{Z}^n} \\mathbb{C} e^{2\\pi i k \\cdot x}\">\\(L^2(\\mathbb{T}^n) = \\bigoplus_{k \\in \\mathbb{Z}^n} \\mathbb{C} e^{2\\pi i k \\cdot x}\\)</span></li>\n<li>Complex structure: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb{T}^2 = \\mathbb{C}/\\Lambda\">\\(\\mathbb{T}^2 = \\mathbb{C}/\\Lambda\\)</span></li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Hatcher, Algebraic Topology</li>\n<li>Siegel, Topics in Complex Function Theory</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-sphere","status":"resolved","id":"ed44d43cf74ca35e","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-sphere]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-sphere","status":"resolved","id":"ed44d43cf74ca35e","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$n\\in\\omega$, $T\\in V$, and $S^1$ is the unit circle supplied by [[58-df-sphere]]","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"\\mathrm{Torus}_S\\subseteq V^{2}","display":false},{"tex":"n\\in\\omega","display":false},{"tex":"T\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"S^1","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Torus}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}torus}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{Torus}_S(T,n)\\leftrightarrow n\\in\\omega\\land T=(S^1)^n","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}torus\\text{-}notation}\\vdash\n\\mathbb T^n\\coloneqq(S^1)^n","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathbb T^n\\cong\\mathbb R^n/\\mathbb Z^n","display":false},{"tex":"\\widehat{\\mathbb{T}^n} \\cong \\mathbb{Z}^n","display":false},{"tex":"L^2(\\mathbb{T}^n) = \\bigoplus_{k \\in \\mathbb{Z}^n} \\mathbb{C} e^{2\\pi i k \\cdot x}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathbb{T}^2 = \\mathbb{C}/\\Lambda","display":false}],"bytes":1213,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-1304","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch19/58-df-torus.md|58-df-torus]]（batch19）"}],"outgoing":["ed44d43cf74ca35e"]}